<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.9.4: Making Sense of Inequalities and Their Solutions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00524</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.9.4: Making Sense of Inequalities and Their Solutions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7660b5bf-aa7c-4ee3-9bac-50247616417b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Use this information to answer questions 1 - 2.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
        <quote id="quote-00001">To help pay for his tuition, a college student plans to work in the evenings and on
        weekends. He has been offered two part-time jobs: working in the guest-services department
        at a hotel and waiting tables at a popular restaurant.</quote>
        <quote id="quote-00002">
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>The job at the hotel pays $18 an hour and offers $33 in transportation allowance per month.</item>
            <item>The job at the restaurant pays $7.50 an hour plus tips. The entire wait staff typically collects about $50 in tips each hour. Tips are divided equally among the 4 wait staff members who share a shift.</item>
          </list>
        </quote>
        <quote id="quote-00003">The equation \( 7.50h +
        \frac {50}{4}h = 18h + 33 \) represents a possible constraint about a situation for 1 month.</quote>
     </para>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q
      #1-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Solve the equation and check your solution.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: \( h=16.5 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00005">\( 7.50h + \frac {50}{4}h = 18h + 33 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00006">\( 7.50(16.5) + \frac {50}{4}(16.5) = 18(16.5) + 33 \)</para>
          <para id="para-00007">\(123.75+206.25=297+33\)</para>
          <para id="para-00008">\(330=330 \checkmark\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!--Q#2-->

      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00009">Add a scale on the number line so that the point marked with a circle represents the
            solution to the equation you found in question 1.
            
              <media alt="A blank number line is shown with an open circle on a point in the middle.
        ">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_09_01.svg"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <para id="para-00010">When you have finished graphing, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00011">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          
            <media alt=" A number line is shown from 14 to 19 with an 
open circle on 16.5.
">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_09_02.jpg"/>
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
        <exercise id="_29538925-54ad-4d51-8b1a-d3614dd56a74" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00013">Which job pays better if he works fewer hours than the solution you found in
              question 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00014">Correct! Hotel Job.</para>
            <para id="para-00015">The correct answer is the hotel job.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--END
      ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q
      #4-->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00016">Explain how you know.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00017">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00018">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The hotel job pays better if he works
            fewer than 16.5 hours a month because I found the pay for both jobs using numbers that
            are less than 16.5 and found that pay at the hotel job is always higher.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->

        <exercise id="_7105cfee-99ee-4db0-9d8f-4882349ffbd7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00019">Which job pays better if he works more hours than the solution you found in
              question 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00020">Correct! Restaurant Job.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">The correct answer is the restaurant job.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--END
      ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q
      #6-->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00022">Explain how you know.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00023">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00024">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The restaurant job pays better if he
            works more than 16.5 hours a month because I found the pay for both jobs using numbers
            that are more than 16.5 and found that pay at the restaurant job is always higher.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!--Q#7-->

      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00025">Draw a number line, including a scale, so that the point marked with a circle
            represents the solution to the inequality: \( 7.50h + \frac {50}{4}h &lt; 18h + 33 \). 
            
              <media alt="A blank number line is shown with an open circle on a point in the middle.
        ">
