      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!--Q#8-->

      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00029">Draw a number line, including a scale, so that the point marked with a circle
            represents the solution to the inequality: \( 7.50h + \frac {50}{4}h > 18h + 33 \). 
            
              <media alt="A blank number line is shown with an open circle on a point in the middle.
        ">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_09_05.svg"/>
              </media>
           </para>
          <para id="para-00030">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
            compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00032">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          
            <media alt="A number line is shown with an open circle on a point in the middle. The number is shaded to the right of the open circle.">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_09_06.jpg"/>
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
      <!--Q#9-->
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00033">Explain how you know.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00034">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00035">Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
          <list id="list-00002">
            <item>Inequality 1 shows the pay at the hotel \( (18h+33) \) being greater than the pay
              at the restaurant \( 7.50h+ \frac{50}{4} \). Earlier, we found out that the hotel job
              is better when the student works less than 16.5 hours. Graph B shows \( h&lt;16.5 \).
              This means Graph B shows the solution to Inequality 1.</item>
            <item>If we substitute a value greater than 16.5 for \( h \), we have a true statement
              for Inequality 2 and a false statement for Inequality 1. This means \( h>16.5 \) is
              a solution to Inequality 2 but not to Inequality 1.</item>
            <item>If we substitute a value less than 16.5 for \( h \), we have a true statement for
              Inequality 1 but not for Inequality 2. So \( h&lt;16.5 \) is a solution to Inequality
              1.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
    </section>
  </content>
